<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	The app's entitlements, currently empty — and deliberately so.

	Both entries this file wants are commented out because the signing team
	(VWRA297FY6) is a *personal* team. Apple refuses both capabilities to a free
	membership, and refuses them at signing time:

	    Cannot create a iOS App Development provisioning profile for
	    "com.evgenij.echo". Personal development teams … do not support the
	    Push Notifications capability.
	    Provisioning profile … doesn't support the group.com.evgenij.echo
	    App Group.

	Uncomment both blocks once a paid Apple Developer Program membership is
	active and the App ID has App Groups and Push Notifications enabled. Nothing
	else has to change: the native and TypeScript halves of both features are
	written and wired, and this file is the only thing standing them down.

	Until then the app builds and installs, screen sharing cannot reach the
	broadcast extension's App Group container, and `request_permission` fails at
	runtime — which the registration hook treats as "no push here" and drops.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		The main app's half of the App Group shared with the broadcast
		extension. See BroadcastExtension/Broadcast.entitlements — the two must
		agree.

	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.evgenij.echo</string>
	</array>
	-->

	<!--
		Required before the app may register for remote notifications; without
		it registration fails at runtime rather than at build time.

		`development` is the value for anything signed with a development
		profile, which is every build this repo produces. Xcode substitutes
		`production` when archiving against a distribution profile, so this
		literal is only ever the debug one. It also decides which APNs host the
		resulting token belongs to — PushPlugin.swift reads it back out of the
		embedded profile rather than guessing.

	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
